      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The boundaries are so-called linear rings, that is, they are closed (not even intersecting) line strings. The outer boundary is distinguished from the inner boundary by the clockwise and counterclockwise directions in which the ring runs, respectively."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Surface consisting of 1 outer boundary and 0 or more inner boundaries. Each internal boundary forms a hole in the polygon."
